---
title: Filter remote jobs to the ones you can actually take
date: 2026-09-09
summary: A new "Eligible for me" toggle in the job search hides postings scoped to a country or region you're not in — without hiding worldwide-remote roles or ones with no location stated at all.
type: changelog
tags:
  - filters
  - job-seekers
draft: false
---

Someone in Indonesia flagged a posting listed as remote that turned out to be open
only to candidates in Canada. Reading the fine print on every "Remote" listing to
check gets old fast, so open [All filters → Location](/jobs) and there's a new
**Eligible for me** pill.

Turn it on and anything scoped to a country or region you're not in drops out of
the list. It leaves worldwide-remote postings alone, and it leaves postings whose
location we could not read from the listing alone too — hiding those would be
worse than showing them, since we genuinely don't know either way.

It's off by default, on purpose. Across the open catalogue, most postings marked
"remote" are actually scoped to one specific country (77.7%) rather than open to
the whole world (9.9%), so switching this on for everyone would have made the list
look broken for anyone outside a handful of countries.

Signed in with a location saved on your profile, it uses that. Otherwise it falls
back to your rough region, the same guess the site already makes elsewhere on
first visit.
